lg-magic (2.0.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Per-remote virtual keyboard/mouse pairs named after the device
    identity ("lg-magicd keyboard/mouse <MAC>"), created before the grab.
  * Held keys are released on a live remap - a map/profile change while a
    key is held can no longer leave the old virtual key stuck.
  * One calibration source per mode: the wizard writes only
    /var/lib/lg-magic/<MAC>/calibration.json in daemon mode; the firmware
    blob stays for the legacy kernel airmouse (raw_only=0).
  * Device identities are validated on the bus (InvalidArguments) and the
    ApiVersion property is exposed; state writes use O_EXCL tmp files;
    the IMU udev rule is restricted to the LG vendor/product.

 -- Ilya Chelyadin <sirfragles@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

lg-magic (2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * v2.0: system daemon with full input takeover and polkit-gated writes.
    - lg-magicd: EVIOCGRAB of the remote, profiles / calibration /
      button mapping / airmouse pipeline, one virtual mouse + keyboard
      (uinput), sd-bus interface org.lgmagic.Manager
    - polkit actions org.lgmagic.{set-config,set-profile,reload};
      the daemon is enabled by the setup wizard, not automatically
    - kernel: raw_only=1 by default (raw decoder; wheel as REL_WHEEL,
      no kernel airmouse); raw_only=0 restores the v1 behaviour
    - CLI: device / profile / button / scroll / diagnose subcommands
      over a dependency-free D-Bus client (lg-magic stays libc/libm)
    - configuration moved from JSON to TOML (lg-magic config migrate)
    - per-device state in /etc/lg-magic/devices.d and /var/lib/lg-magic

 -- Ilya Chelyadin <sirfragles@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 06 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0000

lg-magic (1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: DKMS kernel module + lg-magic userspace tools.
    - C port of the Python tools as a single multi-call binary (no
      Python runtime dependencies)
    - lg-magic setup: interactive configuration and calibration wizard
    - udev rules for the IMU evdev device, hidraw and uinput

 -- Ilya Chelyadin <sirfragles@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 06 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
